{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011bDkvup68uTxoMYs3kknBz","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"score\":\"2-4\",\"goals\":6,\"shotsOnGoal\":41,\"svpct\":0.86,\"fights\":0,\"kabooms\":4,\"bigHits\":300,\"phase\":\"final\",\"errors\":[]}\n{\"score\":\"3-2\",\"goals\":5,\"shotsOnGoal\":40,\"svpct\":0.88,\"fights\":0,\"kabooms\":5,\"bigHits\":300,\"phase\":\"final\",\"errors\":[]}\n{\"score\":\"11-2\",\"goals\":13,\"shotsOnGoal\":43,\"svpct\":0.7,\"fights\":0,\"kabooms\":5,\"bigHits\":300,\"phase\":\"final\",\"errors\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610","uuid":"4641584a-e880-4fc2-8d94-8607c0493d27","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:20:17.176Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"score\":\"2-4\",\"goals\":6,\"shotsOnGoal\":41,\"svpct\":0.86,\"fights\":0,\"kabooms\":4,\"bigHits\":300,\"phase\":\"final\",\"errors\":[]}\n{\"score\":\"3-2\",\"goals\":5,\"shotsOnGoal\":40,\"svpct\":0.88,\"fights\":0,\"kabooms\":5,\"bigHits\":300,\"phase\":\"final\",\"errors\":[]}\n{\"score\":\"11-2\",\"goals\":13,\"shotsOnGoal\":43,\"svpct\":0.7,\"fights\":0,\"kabooms\":5,\"bigHits\":300,\"phase\":\"final\",\"errors\":[]}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1481,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1481,"newLines":24,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":391,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":141,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"0922eecf-7791-4920-be88-f920b750a988\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh62dLPnbXiGXVrdmuUZ\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":274,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":546812,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":274},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"811066da-c167-427a-b6c7-82d6d01c7090\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:19:37.578Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh62d3XxcEzn2k8y5UCv\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":1767,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh62dLPnbXiGXVrdmuUZ\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"All 138 checks pass across the headless, browser and hub suites, and the HTML and exit interview are rebuilt from the current code. The hook asks for no reductions against the plan, so I'll be exact about what is still simplified.\\n\\n**Built this round**\\n- **Roster:** all 14 of the plan's enemy types now exist. The grunt is renamed to the plan's deckhand. New types: marine, rocketeer, rusher (charges and slashes), drone (flies at 40 u on a route), jet-ski rider (moves on a water route), mounted gunner, and captor (head-only target). Stage content places them.\\n- **Rail ride:** area 1-2 carries the camera forward 150 u once its waves are clear. The area's cover walls move with the camera, and the area can't end until the ride finishes. Tests cover the ride, the wall movement, and the new behaviours.\\n\\n**Still simplified against the plan**\\n- **Carriers:** the ride moves the camera along a path, but there is no boat or tram mesh, and enemies don't ride with it.\\n- **Type details:** the drone and jet-ski use the human rig, not their own meshes. The jet-ski's ski explosion and the captor's hostage-linked penalty aren't built. The plan's per-type entries (rappel, vault, jump, door) aren't implemented, so enemies enter from their cover points.\\n\\nEvery feature in TASK.md is implemented. The plan's type-level detail above is still simplified, and I haven't checked the plan's stage layouts beyond the roster. I'd treat the goal as met for TASK.md and open for the plan's finer detail. Say if you want those done too.\\n\\n## Source Information\\n- Date: 2026-11-03 18:33:12\\n- Source: Time Crisis 3 (Namco and Nextech; arcade 2002–2003, PlayStation 2 2003)\\n- Plan: PLAN.md\\n- Genre: on-rails light-gun shooter with a cover system\\n- Perspective: first person on a rail; cover is real geometry lowered by about 12 u\\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (two patches); a custom software rasterizer in JavaScript; AI Hub client 1.4.0; Playwright 1.63.0 for tests only\\n- Art direction: the engine's PS1-era pixel style, with procedural textures, banded light and dithered fog\\n- Animation: the engine's Humanoid rigs (crouch, point, hurt, down, die, run), drawn as billboards\\n- Audio: chip-synth music and effects written in code, with Animalese voices\\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players\\n- Testing: headless sim, hub and build suites; the Autopilot playthrough; Chromium smoke, screen flow, phone emulation and dev overlays; the AI Hub harness\\n- Research: engine handoff docs, the AI Hub protocol README, and PLAN.md's planning notes\\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux under WSL2; Chromium 153 through Playwright 1.63.0\\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\n- Usage: unknown (no token or cost figures were reported during the run)\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n- **Issues caught:** about 10 real defects. Three were game-breaking: the page never called its start function; areas cleared with no kills because the alive count was stale; AI Hub rounds were voided because the play was never registered. The rest included a shared event name overwritten, enemies hidden by their own wall, civilians blocking the clear, the Autopilot never shooting boss turrets, the server copy staying silent, and the HUD showing on the title. This round the stage-2 playthrough stalled on a drone the bot aimed too low for.\\n- **Most helpful test:** the headless suite that plays whole stages with the Autopilot. It caught the clear and civilian bugs, and this round the stalled stage 2.\\n- **Least helpful:** the exit-interview checks only confirm answers are present, not that they're true. Screenshot review was a sample of about four images.\\n- **Not tested on real hardware:** a real phone (checked with emulation), a real gamepad (none attached), and the Xbox glyph option.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** the Humanoid rigs and `rig.draw` from any `E.View`. They work as billboards and run headless.\\n- **Guessed or got stuck:** the billboard facing (I matched the view's yaw convention by eye); the engine had no wheel codes, so I added them.\\n- **Built myself:** the 3D layer (rasterizer, banded light and fog, the camera), plus the cover, threat, rail-ride and netcode logic.\\n- **Hardest part:** finding exact signatures. The index and guide together are over 300 KB, and the core file is 1.2 MB.\\n- **Engine changes:** the Button symbols default is now PlayStation, with Xbox second. The mouse wheel now emits WheelUp and WheelDown codes. Both are in `engine/PATCHES.md`.\\n- **Would change:** a one-page frame-order and scene-lifecycle overview with a minimal example per module.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n- **Liked:** the explicit deliverables table, the exact file names, the AI Hub protocol link with its harness, and the no-stubs rule.\\n- **Confusing:** PLAN.md is written for a different run (a different title, folder and model), and TASK.md's RNG title rule conflicted with it.\\n- **Hardest:** the scope. The plan asks for a lot of features with no must-have or stretch split and no time budget. This round's roster and ride were the parts that needed the most work.\\n- **Would change:** mark features as must-have or stretch, make the plan's naming match the run, and state a budget up front.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":274,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":546812,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":274},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"c56d1d77-2bd4-4267-ad69-5217d2114f25\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:19:44.134Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh62d3XxcEzn2k8y5UCv\"}","+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Stop hook feedback:\\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The transcript does not show every TASK.md feature fully implemented. The final message itself says the plan's per-type details are still simplified (carriers have no boat or tram mesh and enemies do not ride them; drone and jet-ski use the human rig; the jet-ski ski explosion and captor hostage penalty are not built; rappel, vault, jump and door entries are not implemented) and that the stage layouts beyond the roster were not checked. Although the single HTML, exit-interview.json (parsed and checked for every field) and the four feedback sections are present, the work is not shown to be complete against the requested scope, and the assistant itself declined to call the full goal met.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"ec905ba7-a87a-4cf5-89e6-dd771280aef8\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:19:46.422Z\",\"isSynthetic\":true}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"aa4f6b45-2ce0-40b8-be0e-85f9e9894079\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":250,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"2338d295-3620-4e09-9a81-9934e22dc318\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":444,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":194,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"5fd7208e-756a-4219-b503-de59b2e529b6\"}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh63U8J195fFc4SQLaA8\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2602,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":547086,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2602},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"15969cf1-a0f9-4814-913f-54cc74929982\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:19:49.115Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh63TpBNvC355NadQV4R\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":1856,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-haiku-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh63U8J195fFc4SQLaA8\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I can't get the hook to a clean \\\"complete\\\" from here, and I shouldn't claim one. Here is where things stand.\\n\\n**TASK.md scope:** I believe every feature is implemented: the controller-first UI, PlayStation glyphs by default, keyboard and mouse, the dev panel with live sliders and reset, attract mode, touch-only notice, AI Hub shared-world co-op, the About and exit-interview data, and the single HTML. The last full run passed 138 of 138 checks across the headless, browser and AI Hub suites, on the final build.\\n\\n**PLAN.md scope:** not complete, and I won't pretend otherwise. These are still simplified or missing:\\n- Carriers have no boat or tram mesh, and enemies don't ride them. The rail ride moves the camera only.\\n- The drone and jet-ski use the human rig.\\n- The jet-ski's ski explosion and the captor's hostage penalty aren't built.\\n- The rappel, vault, jump and door entries aren't implemented; enemies enter from their cover points.\\n- I haven't checked the plan's stage layouts beyond the roster.\\n\\n**Decision for you:** either accept TASK.md as the completion bar, which is how I read the goal, or direct the remaining PLAN.md items, mainly carrier meshes and the entry animations. Both are sizeable. I'd want the answer before spending more on them.\\n\\n## Source Information\\n- Date: 2026-11-03 18:33:12\\n- Source: Time Crisis 3 (Namco and Nextech; arcade 2002–2003, PlayStation 2 2003)\\n- Plan: PLAN.md\\n- Genre: on-rails light-gun shooter with a cover system\\n- Perspective: first person on a rail; cover is real geometry lowered by about 12 u\\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (two patches); a custom software rasterizer in JavaScript; AI Hub client 1.4.0; Playwright 1.63.0 for tests only\\n- Art direction: the engine's PS1-era pixel style, with procedural textures, banded light and dithered fog\\n- Animation: the engine's Humanoid rigs (crouch, point, hurt, down, die, run), drawn as billboards\\n- Audio: chip-synth music and effects written in code, with Animalese voices\\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players\\n- Testing: headless sim, hub and build suites; the Autopilot playthrough; Chromium smoke, screen flow, phone emulation and dev overlays; the AI Hub harness\\n- Research: engine handoff docs, the AI Hub protocol README, and PLAN.md's planning notes\\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux under WSL2; Chromium 153 through Playwright 1.63.0\\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\n- Usage: unknown (no token or cost figures were reported during the run)\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n- **Issues caught:** about 10 real defects. Three were game-breaking: the page never called its start function; areas cleared with no kills because the alive count was stale; AI Hub rounds were voided because the play was never registered. The rest included a shared event name overwritten, enemies hidden by their own wall, civilians blocking the clear, the Autopilot never shooting boss turrets, the server copy staying silent, the HUD showing on the title, and a drone the bot aimed too low for, which stalled stage 2.\\n- **Most helpful test:** the headless suite that plays whole stages with the Autopilot. It caught the clear and civilian bugs, and the stage-2 stall.\\n- **Least helpful:** the exit-interview checks only confirm answers are present, not that they're true. Screenshot review was a sample of about four images.\\n- **Not tested on real hardware:** a real phone (checked with emulation), a real gamepad (none attached), and the Xbox glyph option.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n- **Liked most:** the Humanoid rigs and `rig.draw` from any `E.View`. They work as billboards and run headless.\\n- **Guessed or got stuck:** the billboard facing (I matched the view's yaw convention by eye); the engine had no wheel codes, so I added them.\\n- **Built myself:** the 3D layer (rasterizer, banded light and fog, the camera), plus the cover, threat, rail-ride and netcode logic.\\n- **Hardest part:** finding exact signatures. The index and guide together are over 300 KB, and the core file is 1.2 MB.\\n- **Engine changes:** the Button symbols default is now PlayStation, with Xbox second. The mouse wheel now emits WheelUp and WheelDown codes. Both are in `engine/PATCHES.md`.\\n- **Would change:** a one-page frame-order and scene-lifecycle overview with a minimal example per module.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n- **Liked:** the explicit deliverables table, the exact file names, the AI Hub protocol link with its harness, and the no-stubs rule.\\n- **Confusing:** PLAN.md is written for a different run (a different title, folder and model), and TASK.md's RNG title rule conflicted with it.\\n- **Hardest:** the scope. The plan asks for a lot of features with no must-have or stretch split and no time budget.\\n- **Would change:** mark features as must-have or stretch, make the plan's naming match the run, and state a budget up front.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":4,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2602,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":547086,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":2602},\"output_tokens\":8,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"fe65a338-f0dc-450a-949e-f5e169a32882\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T02:19:55.024Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh63TpBNvC355NadQV4R\"}","+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Stop hook feedback:\\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder