in under fireworks; Krake's broadcast plays on the festival's giant screens (a live portrait texture); they dock at Lantern Pier | — | — | lines in §5.9 |\\n| **1-1 LANTERN PIER** | 45 | A 7.5-m wooden pier lined with lantern stalls; the warehouses of the quay ahead (x 380). P1 hides behind stacked fish crates, P2 behind barrels and a bollard (the schema example in §4.10) | (a) 3 deckhands pop up behind stalls; (b) one comes out of the warehouse door, one jumps off a fishing boat's \\n| **1-2 FISH MARKET** | 50 | Travel: along the quay, then Rook kicks in a side door. Inside, a brick hall with a tiled floor, wooden stalls, ice tables, hanging paper lanterns and an upper gallery | (a) 4 deckhands, 2 of them on the gallery, who fall when killed; (b) **the first Red Tide** rolls out from behind the ice table; (c\\n| **1-3 CONTAINER YARD** | 60 | Berth 9: container stacks (red, blue, ochre, green), a gantry crane, sodium lamps, forklifts | (a) 3 deckhands jump down off containers and 2 hide behind forklifts; (b) **BULLDOG**, an armored truck, smashes through a container wall: its gunner (3 HP, above the gun shield, 50% threat), then its fu\\n| **1-4 CANAL RUN** (moving) | 60 | Mari drives through the Silver Canals under festival bridges; duck behind the boat's armored gunwale (part of the carrier); spray, sway | 3 pairs of jet skis from side canals; bridge gunners on 2 bridges, with deckhands on the railings who fall into the water; a quartermaster on a moored boat \\n| **1-B BOSS: STINGRAY → BARRACUDA** | 100 | The harbor mouth, the two boats side by side; cover behind the gunwale | §5.7 | the boss framework, torpedoes | — |\\n| **1-Z outro** | — | Barracuda falls into the sea; the Stingray explodes; Juno traces Krake's signal | — | — | STAGE CLEAR → results |\\n\\n### 5.5 Stage 2, STORM SIGNAL (Gull's Rest and Lighthouse Point, 02:10, thunderstorm)\\n**Look**:\\n- slate and green-grey, with heavy rain (screen streaks and splashes);\\n- lightning every 9–15 s: the sky flashes, a white `game.flash` at 0.25, thunder after 0.5–1.5 s;\\n- fog `#26343c` 200–1200;\\n- timber and plaster houses with slate roofs; wet stone (a `wet` overlay pattern that brightens lit bands);\\n- fishermen in yellow raincoats;\\n- the lighthouse beam sweeps every 8 s: a visible cone of glowing lines and a dynamic light.\\n\\nMusic: \\\"Storm Signal\\\".\\n\\n| Scene | Time | Setting and cover | Waves | New | Objects and cues |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| **2-0 intro** | — | The boat docks in the rain; lightning shows the lighthouse; Krake's radio intercept and Hammerhead's reply | — | — | — |\\n| **2-1 GULL'S REST** | 50 | A steep cobbled lane, timber houses, washing lines, boats up on blocks; cover behind a fish cart and a stone well | (a) deckhands in windows (the glass breaks); (b) **rushers**, 2 then 3, sprinting down the lane; (c) a quartermaster from an alley drops the **SHOTGUN +8** (\\\"NEW WEAPON\\\"); marines behin\\n| **2-2 NET LOFTS** | 55 | Inside a tall wooden loft: stairs, hanging nets (`alphaTest`), fish-oil barrels | (a) a **shield** trooper advances down the stairs (\\\"Shotgun! Knock that shield aside!\\\"); (b) 3 **rappellers** drop through a roof hatch; (c) 2 Red Tide and a grenadier on the upper floor | shields, rappelling | the fish-o\\n| **2-3 FUNICULAR** (moving) | 60 | The cliff funicular climbs through the storm; duck behind the car's bench and bulkhead | deckhands on the cliff-path terraces; **the passing car**: the descending car crosses with 3 gunners in a 4-s window; at the top station the car stops for **THE GULL**: a laser sniper among 3 perches on th\\n| **2-4 LIGHTHOUSE KEEP** | 60 | The courtyard, the keeper's house, the lighthouse door; then up the **spiral stairs** (vertical travel; shoot upward) | (a) marines and a Red Tide; (b) **hostage**: a captor holds Dr. Tejada at the door (\\\"One more step and the old man swims!\\\"); his head shows for 0.7-s windows; (c) rushers and de\\n| **2-B BOSS: HAMMERHEAD** | 120 |