{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The condition requires that every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, and the transcript shows gaps. TASK.md asks for a Research note, a 'Performance' section, and a 'Testing' section that calls for testing parameters to be kept behind one command; those are present. But the transcript shows features that were only partly done: the Online section says the hub harness 'only proves the protocol' and no real multi-device session was played; the About pages, which TASK.md requires to hold the four feedback sections, were written before the final test run and remain partly generic placeholder-style text (e.g. 'See the final report.' was replaced, but earlier drafts had such stubs), and the Testing Feedback counts ('About 25 real issues') and the drill/story checks were acknowledged as partly test-setup driven rather than demonstrating play. The engine's own check tool still reported look notes that were not acted on. Also, the final reply and exit-interview.json were written from an intermediate state, and the transcript never shows a fresh confirmation that the exit-interview.json contents match the final About text after the last edits. Therefore the transcript does not show clear evidence that every feature is implemented with no stubs, so the condition is not verifiably satisfied."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610","uuid":"af3f3f74-84d8-40ea-b476-d981d4fa9378","t