whether the plan's scale (dozens of systems) should be trimmed for a lower effort level, and give a usage or time budget so scope can be matched to it.\"]],","   ['ENGINE CHANGES', ['- Font: PlayStation face-button symbols added to the 5x7 font (they printed as ?).', '- Gamepad: Options is ignored while Create is held (AI Hub owns Create + Options).',"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-182910__x9a2bbb/work/IceHoc-Kaboom-IceHockey-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-182910/hub/game.html","hunks":[{"oldStart":15679,"oldLines":7,"newStart":15679,"newLines":7,"lines":["     'Every song, sound effect and voice is synthesized in code: no audio files. Voices are gibberish babble.', 'All art is drawn by code: the engine\\'s procedural HD Humanoid rigs plus new hockey gear, rinks, crowds and effects. Props from the engine\\'s core library.',","     'The Mukluk Falls Muskrats, Coach Marge, Old Gus, Doris, Goldie Glitterman and every team in this game are fictional.']],","   ['SOURCE INFORMATION', [\"- Date: 2026-11-03 18:29:10\", \"- Source: Ice hockey (over-the-top arcade style)\", \"- Plan: PLAN.md\", \"- Genre: Arcade sports: 3-on-3 ice hockey with goalies, a fight minigame, a 5-chapter story campaign (the Cup Run), exhibition, practice drills, 1-4 player versus\", \"- Perspective: 2.5D TV broadcast camera (engine threequarter view, pitch 55) tracking the puck; Overhead option (topdown); ice-level brawler view for fights, replays and player intros\", \"- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full engine, patched: font symbols, hub controller rule, Humanoid gear hook, organ/brass waves, lowpass, voice bus, dialog voice hook); plain JavaScript, one self-contained HTML file; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 (Chromium) for tests\", \"- Art direction: The engine's native PS1-era pixel art (ps1 resolution, expand) with HD Humanoid rigs, plus code-drawn hockey sticks, skates, helmets with visors, goalie pads/blocker/catcher/cage, jersey numbers, procedural team logos, five dressed arenas (stands and fans, boards, translucent breakable glass, nets, props, lights) and effects\", \"- Animation: The engine's procedural Humanoid rigs, with a solvePose overlay for skating strides, crossovers, hockey stops, backward skating, stick handling, passes, wrist and slap shots, checks, pokes, deke spins, goalie stances and saves, celebrations; engine moves (jab, haymaker, hook), guard stance, down/cheer poses for fights and reactions\", \"- Audio: All in code: chip-synth music in the engine's song format (theme, menu, locker room, pond, Grindhouse, mall, final, play with drive/KABOOM/fight layers, a Flood Wagon waltz, victory, defeat, credits), organ stings, synthesized sfx (post ping, slapshot, glass shatter, goal horn, buzzer, whistle), a crowd bed with reactions, and Animalese-style formant babble voices per character\", \"- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared-world, 1-4 seats: host-run match, client intents at 15 Hz with press counters, 15 Hz snapshots, interpolation and own-skater prediction, own game card, finish with standings, scores, stats and awards; plus local 1-4 players on one machine\", \"- Testing: Headless Node suites driving the game with game.advance and game.debug (units, systems, 4 players, determinism, dev mode, attract mode, all 7 drills, AI balance, a scripted playthrough of the whole story with a bot, text pools) plus Playwright browser checks (pages, menus, mouse hover and click, glyphs, touch-only) and the AI Hub harness in 5 configurations, all behind node tests/run.mjs; screenshots reviewed by eye\", \"- Research: Read the engine handoff docs (README, API.md, AI_GUIDE sections, sports kit, engine source for font, glyphs, Humanoid, audio, Dialog) and the AI Hub protocol README and harness; no web research on hockey\", \"- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\", \"- Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\", \"- Usage: unknown\"]],","-  ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [\"- Issues caught: About 25 real issues: a name clash that crashed the floor bake (only visible in a browser), shots and AI actions blocked in the shootout phase, AI shooters losing their wind-up during hockey stops, goalies saving nearly everything, cross-crease one-timers never scoring, too many hockey stops and too many KABOOMs, the drill and faceoff edge cases, a lost tap during hit-stop, a missing showcase shootout, and several test-setup mistakes.\", \"- Critical: 4 were game breaking: the floor-bake crash (black screen in the browser), the shootout that never ended because shooters could not shoot, goals almost never happening in AI games, and a faceoff crash when a team had no skaters on the ice.\", \"- Most helpful test: The scripted whole-story playthrough with the bot plus the AI-vs-AI balance run: together they exercise every system end to end and caught the shootout and scoring problems.\", \"- Least helpful test: The engine check tool's flat-color look notes: an ice rink is legitimately mostly one bright color, so those notes were noise.\"]],","+  ['TESTING FEEDBACK', [\"- Issues caught: About 26 real issues: arena lamps blowing the ice out to pure white (hiding its texture and the center-ice logo), a name clash that crashed the floor bake (only visible in a browser), shots and AI actions blocked in the shootout phase, AI shooters losing their wind-up during hockey stops, goalies saving nearly everything, cross-crease one-timers never scoring, too many hockey stops and too many KABOOMs, the drill and faceoff edge cases, a lost tap during hit-stop, a missing showcase shootout, and several test-setup mistakes.\", \"- Critical: 4 were game breaking: the floor-bake crash (black screen in the browser), the shootout that never ended because shooters could not shoot, goals almost never happening in AI games, and a faceoff crash when a team had no skaters on the ice.\", \"- Most helpful test: The scripted whole-story playthrough with the bot plus the AI-vs-AI balance run: together they exercise every system end to end and caught the shootout and scoring problems.\", \"- Least helpful test: The determinism check (same seed twice, same game): it never failed, so it found nothing, though it guards the replays and attract mode. (The engine check tool's flat-color notes looked like noise at first, but they led me to the blown-out ice lighting.)\"]],","   ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', [\"- Liked most: The procedural Humanoid rigs: dressing and posing skaters, goalies, referees and the cast in code, with live portraits for dialog, gave a lot of character for free, and the fixed-step headless game made testing cheap.\", \"- Stuck or guessed wrong: Yes: the threequarter view's base scale of 1.5 meant zoom 1 was far too close for a rink; hit-stop from hitFx swallows taps; changing zoom re-bakes the floor, so a continuous zoom was not an option; and px.sprite's scale placement took trial and error.\", \"- Built myself: The hockey simulation itself: skating physics, the substepped puck against curved boards, posts and nets, the goalie save solver, and the arena drawing (stands, boards, breakable glass panels, nets).\", \"- Hardest part: Depth ordering custom 3D-ish geometry (boards, glass, nets, stands) with the queue/decal model, and keeping the floor bake cheap.\", \"- Changed in the engine: Five small patches: PlayStation symbols in the font, Options ignored while Create is held (AI Hub), a Humanoid gear hook for sticks and goalie gear, organ/brass waves plus lowpass and a voice bus in audio, and a per-letter function voice in Dialog.\", \"- One change: A first-class hook for held items and attachments on the Humanoid (sticks, bats, rackets) with hand placement, instead of only sword, gun and staff.\"]],","   ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', [\"- Liked most: The clear separation of what to build (TASK.md) from how (a detailed plan), and the concrete done criteria: dev mode with sliders, attract mode, hub play, the feedback sections.\", \"- Confusing: The plan's file names used the max-effort run's suffix while TASK.md gave the medium one; TASK.md won. 'Online' points at the hub library rather than saying shared-world, which the plan settled.\", \"- Hardest: Fitting the full feature list (story, 5 arenas, 7 drills, fights, shootout, online, dev mode, attract mode) into one coherent, tested build at once.\", \"- Would change: Say whether the plan's scale (dozens of systems) should be trimmed for a lower effort level, and give a usage or time budget so scope can be matched to it.\"]],","   ['ENGINE CHANGES', ['- Font: PlayStation face-button symbols added to the 5x7 font (they printed as ?).', '- Gamepad: Options is ignored while Create is held (AI Hub owns Create + Options).',"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-182910__x9a2bbb/work/IceHoc-Kaboom-IceHockey-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-182910/src/08-about.js","hunks":[{"oldStart":4,"oldLines":7,"newStart":4,"newLines":7,"lines":["     'Every song, sound effect and voice is synthesized in code: no audio files. Voices are gibberish babble.', 'All art is drawn by code: the engine\\'s procedural HD Humanoid rigs plus new hockey gear, rinks, crowds and effects. Props from the engine\\'s core library.',","     'The Mukluk Falls Muskrats, Coach Marge, Old Gus, Doris, Goldie Glitterman and every team in this game are fictional.']],","   ['SOURCE INFORMATION', [\"- Date: 2026-11-03 18:29:10\", \"- Source: Ice hockey (over-the-top arcade style)\", \"- Plan: PLAN.md\", \"- Genre: Arcade sports: 3-on-3 ice hockey with goalies, a fight minigame, a 5-chapter story campaign (the Cup Run), exhibition, practice drills, 1-4 player versus\", \"- Perspective: 2.5D TV broadcast camera (engine threequarter view, pitch 55) tracking the puck; Overhead option (topdown); ice-level brawler view for fights, replays and player intros\", \"- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full engine, patched: font symbols,