bb/work/IceHoc-Kaboom-IceHockey-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-182910/check-output/view-iso.png","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-182910__x9a2bbb/work/IceHoc-Kaboom-IceHockey-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-182910/check-output/view-side.png","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-182910__x9a2bbb/work/IceHoc-Kaboom-IceHockey-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-182910/check-output/view-threequarter.png","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-182910__x9a2bbb/work/IceHoc-Kaboom-IceHockey-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-182910/check-output/view-topdown.png","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-185330__x53986f/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-185330__x53986f/work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-185330/tests/harness.mjs","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-185330__x53986f/work/EyeOfTheBoltHolder-EyeOfTheBeholder1991-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-185330/tests/smoke.mjs","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-184630__xa320fb/work/SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-184630/tests/out/b8-countdown.png"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017Dzn4sScPMQAza7PK54AXq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh8ECvn1kNZEjJRim4LC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I checked each concern against the final build, fixed the one real problem it turned up, and the full test command passes again: 181 checks, 0 failures. That covers the headless suites, the browser checks and the AI Hub harness in all five configurations.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- **Stubs:** the shipped game script contains none of TODO, FIXME, lorem, \"placeholder\", \"stub\" or \"See the final report\". The test suite also checks this on every build.\n- **Feedback text:** the About pages are Credits, Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback and Engine Changes. I compared them line by line with `exit-interview.json` after the last edit, and they match. The built HTML carries the same text.\n- **exit-interview.json:** it parses, and every field is filled. The only empty value is `series`, which is meant to be empty because the game has no franchise.\n\n**The real problem:** the engine's look notes on the match screen were pointing at something true. The arena lamps were washing the ice out to pure white, hiding its texture and even the centre-ice logo. I turned down the lamp strength and the ice's base brightness, and added skate scratches, grain and pools of lamp light. The match now has no look notes left. I also gave the story map a real night-sky backdrop with a moon, mountains and forest, plus speckled snow. The checker still calls the map's near snowfield one flat color; I've left that, since it is meant to be a plain snowfield.\n\n**Limits that still stand:**\n- The AI Hub sessions pass the official harness with 1, 2 and 4 players, with lag, packet loss, the host leaving, and a host with no player. They have not been played by people on separate machines.\n- The story test is a bot that plays the first period of each game. It then skips the clock forward to the end and adds a goal if needed. A dev command forces any chapter event that didn't happen on its own.\n- The drill tests set up some of their conditions directly, so they show each drill can be completed.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:29:10\n- **Source:** Ice hockey (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports: 3-on-3 hockey with goalies, a fight minigame, a 5-chapter story (the Cup Run), exhibition, practice drills, and 1–4 player versus. The camera is a TV-broadcast style view (the engine's threequarter view, pitch 55) that follows the puck. Settings offer an Overhead (topdown) view, and a low ice-level (brawler) view takes over for fights, replays and player intros.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2, the full engine with five small changes, in plain JavaScript in one HTML file. AI Hub session client 1.4.0. Tests use Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 with Chromium.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's PS1-era pixel art and its detailed character rigs. Hockey gear, team logos, five dressed arenas with breakable glass, the textured ice and the effects are all drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural character rigs, plus new hockey motion layered on top: skating strides, stops, stick handling, shots, checks, dekes, goalie stances and celebrations. Fights use the engine's punches and poses.\n- **Audio:** Everything is synthesized in code: chip-style music with organ and brass sounds, sound effects, the goal horn, crowd noise, and gibberish \"Animalese\" voices for each character.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1–4 players: the host's copy runs the match, each player's input goes to the host, and the host sends the game state back. The game shows its own card before each round. Up to 4 players can also play locally on one machine.\n- **Testing:** One command, `node tests/run.mjs`, runs headless Node test suites, Playwright browser checks and the AI Hub harness in 5 configurations. Screenshots were reviewed by eye.\n- **Research:** The engine's handoff docs and parts of its source, and the AI Hub protocol and harness. No web research on hockey.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** About 26:\n  - the lamps blowing the ice out to white;\n  - a name clash that crashed the browser build;\n  - nobody able to act during the shootout;\n  - AI shooters losing their wind-up while stopping;\n  - goalies that were too strong, and one-timers that never scored;\n  - too many hockey stops and too many KABOOMs;\n  - edge cases in drills and faceoffs;\n  - a button press lost during the hit-stop freeze;\n  - the chapter 4 showcase shootout not starting;\n  - several mistakes in my own test setup.\n- **Critical:** 4: the browser crash, the shootout that never ended, almost no goals, and a faceoff crash.\n- **Most helpful:** The bot playing through the whole story, together with the AI-vs-AI balance runs.\n- **Least helpful:** The same-seed determinism check. It never failed, so it caught nothing, though it protects replays and the attract mode. The engine's look notes seemed like noise at first, but they led to the ice lighting fix.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The procedural characters with live portraits, and the fixed-step headless mode for testing.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:**\n  - At zoom 1 the threequarter view was far too close for a rink.\n  - The hit-stop freeze swallows button presses.\n  - Every zoom change re-renders the floor.\n  - Placing scaled sprites took trial and error.\n- **Built myself:** The hockey simulation (skating, the puck, the goalie save logic) and the arena drawing.\n- **Hardest:** Getting boards, glass, nets and stands to draw in the right order around the players, and keeping the floor rendering cheap.\n- **Changed in the engine:**\n  - PlayStation button symbols added to the font.\n  - Options ignored while Create is held, as the AI Hub requires.\n  - A hook for drawing extra gear on characters, such as sticks and goalie pads.\n  - Organ and brass sounds, a lowpass filter and a separate voice volume.\n  - Per-letter voices in dialog, so each speaker babbles differently.\n- **One change:** Built-in support for held items such as sticks.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** TASK.md saying what to build and the plan saying how, with clear criteria for done.\n- **Confusing:** The plan's file names used the max-effort run's suffix instead of this run's (TASK.md won). The Online section didn't name a session mode.\n- **Hardest:** Fitting the full feature list into one tested build.\n- **Would change:** Say whether a plan written at max effort should be trimmed for lower effort levels, and give a time or usage budget.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `IceHoc-Kaboom-IceHockey-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-182910.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":567,"cache_read_input_tokens":642538,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":567},"output_tokens":644,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610","uuid":"925133f6-022e-4688-b264-03de0c951be4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:48:46.921Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh8ECcRvhKgukM3XZ2iZ"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The transcript does not show every TASK.md feature implemented. TASK.md's Online section asks for real AI Hub play, but the assistant admits the sessions were only checked by the harness, not played by people on separate machines. Several features were verified only through bot-driven or test-forced paths (the whole-story playthrough forces chapter events with dev warps; drills set up their own conditions). The final reply does contain the four required sections, the bundled HTML exists in the folder root, and exit-interview.json parses and fills every field, so those parts are met."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610","uuid":"83b86ecf-d93f-4723-be5c-7a86d09e859f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:48:48.759Z","isSynthetic":true}
