{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghDjM26Ap7YuJ4N52VNe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing changed this turn and no new tests were run. The one remaining objection, people playing the game on separate machines, is something I can't do from here, and TASK.md doesn't ask for it.\n\n**What TASK.md asks for online.** The Multiplayer line says \"Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\" That means building to the AI Hub Session Protocol and passing the hub's harness, which the protocol defines as its library test. The game does both:\n- It connects as a shared-world session and shows its own card.\n- The host runs the match while the other copies send their player's input and draw the host's game.\n- Players who leave are taken over by the computer, and results go to the hub.\n- It passes the harness with 1, 2 and 4 players, with lag and packet loss, when the host leaves, and with a host that has no player.\n- A two-copy session driven by real key presses confirms remote players control their own skaters.\n- It also has local play for 1–4 people on one machine.\n\n**What I can't do.** Recruiting people to play on separate devices is a human playtest, not a feature I can implement. I'm saying so plainly rather than claiming it happened. If that playtest is required, someone with two devices will need to run it on the live hub.\n\nThe other conditions hold: the single HTML file is in the folder root, `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled, and the game contains no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. The last full test run passed 183 checks with 0 failures.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:29:10\n- **Source:** Ice hockey (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports: 3-on-3 hockey with goalies, a fight minigame, a 5-chapter story, exhibition, practice drills and 1–4 player versus. The camera is a TV-broadcast view that follows the puck, with an Overhead option and an ice-level view for fights, replays and player intros.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the full engine with 5 small changes), plain JavaScript in one HTML file, AI Hub session client 1.4.0. Tests use Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 with Chromium.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's PS1-era pixel art and detailed characters. Everything hockey is drawn in code: gear, team logos, five arenas with breakable glass, lit textured ice and effects.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural characters plus new hockey motion: skating, stops, stick handling, shots, checks, dekes, goalie stances and celebrations. Fights use the engine's own punches and poses.\n- **Audio:** All made in code: chiptune music with organ and brass sounds, sound effects, the goal horn, crowd noise and gibberish voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1–4 players, run by the host's copy, with the game's own card; plus local play for 1–4 on one machine.\n- **Testing:** One command, `node tests/run.mjs`, runs:\n  - headless suites that drive the game directly;\n  - all 7 drills played through controller input only;\n  - each chapter played without forcing any events;\n  - browser checks;\n  - the AI Hub harness in 5 configurations;\n  - a two-copy hub session driven by real key presses.\n\n  I also reviewed screenshots by eye.\n- **Research:** The engine's docs and source, and the AI Hub protocol and harness. No web research on hockey.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 35; the list is in `exit-interview.json`.\n- **How many were critical?** Five:\n  - remote players' input never reached their skaters;\n  - a crash in the browser;\n  - a shootout that never ended;\n  - almost no goals in AI-vs-AI games;\n  - a faceoff crash when a team had no skaters on the ice.\n- **What was the most helpful test?** The two-copy hub session driven by real key presses. It caught the remote-input bug, which the harness checks missed.\n- **What was the least helpful test?** The check that the same seed gives the same game, which never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** The procedural characters with live portraits, and the fixed-step headless mode for testing.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n  - The broadcast view was far too close at zoom 1.\n  - The hit-stop freeze swallows button presses.\n  - Every zoom change re-renders the floor.\n  - Placing scaled sprites took trial and error.\n- **What did you have to build yourself?** The hockey simulation and the arena drawing.\n- **What was hardest?** Getting the boards, glass and nets to layer correctly in front of and behind the players.\n- **What did you change in the engine?**\n  - PlayStation button symbols in the font.\n  - Options ignored while Create is held, as the hub requires.\n  - A hook for drawing gear on characters.\n  - Organ and brass sounds, a lowpass filter and a separate voice volume.\n  - Per-letter dialog voices.\n- **What one change would you make?** Built-in support for held items such as sticks.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** TASK.md says what to build, the plan says how, and the criteria for done are clear.\n- **What was confusing?** The plan used the max-effort run's file names (I followed TASK.md), and the Online section doesn't name a session mode.\n- **What was hardest?** Getting the full feature list into one tested build.\n- **What would you change?** Say whether a max-effort plan should be trimmed for lower effort levels, and give a time or usage budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2357,"cache_read_input_tokens":702971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2357},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610","uuid":"15000ecf-fa66-40ce-9328-db65d0c0e20a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:00:53.242Z","request_id":"req_011CghDjLji9eqNyd5NDQgLE"}
