{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghDvQXEU8wCNrHGioUwd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ran the AI Hub's own library-admission check, `scripts/hub-check.mjs` from the ai-hub repo, and the game passed all 6 runs and 86 checks. This is the check the hub uses to decide whether a game may join the library. It played the game at 2, 3 and 4 players on a poor network (150 ms lag, packet loss). It also covered the host leaving, a dedicated-server host with no player, and the game opened on its own outside a session.\n\nIt ran on a byte-identical copy of the deliverable. After it passed I changed only the About and exit-interview Testing text to record the result, and rebuilt. I didn't re-run the hub check after that text-only rebuild.\n\nMy first attempt failed two \"outside a session\" checks. That was my mistake: the script serves its own folder, so the path I gave it loaded a not-found page instead of the game. Pointing it at a server holding the game fixed it.\n\nThat leaves the earlier evidence unchanged: the full test command's last run passed 183 checks with 0 failures. It includes a two-copy hub session driven by real key presses, which is how I found and fixed a bug where remote players couldn't control their skaters.\n\nWhat I still can't provide is people playing on separate machines. That's a human playtest, not something I can arrange from here.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:29:10\n- **Source:** Ice hockey (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports: 3-on-3 hockey with goalies, a fight minigame, a 5-chapter story, exhibition, practice drills, and 1–4 player versus. The camera is a TV-broadcast view that follows the puck, with an Overhead option and an ice-level view for fights, replays and intros.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the full engine, with 5 small changes), plain JavaScript in one HTML file, AI Hub session client 1.4.0. Tests use Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 with Chromium.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native PS1-era pixel art and detailed characters. Everything hockey-specific is drawn in code: gear, team logos, five arenas with breakable glass, lit textured ice, and effects.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural characters, plus new hockey motion: skating, stops, stick handling, shots, checks, dekes, goalie stances and celebrations. Fights use the engine's own punches and poses.\n- **Audio:** All made in code: chiptune music with organ and brass sounds, sound effects, the goal horn, crowd noise, and gibberish voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1–4 players: the host's copy runs the game, and the game shows its own lobby card. Local play for 1–4 players on one machine too.\n- **Testing:** One command, `node tests/run.mjs`, covers:\n  - headless suites (no browser);\n  - all 7 drills played through controller input only;\n  - each chapter played without forcing anything;\n  - browser checks;\n  - the AI Hub harness in 5 configurations;\n  - a two-copy hub session driven by real key presses.\n\n  Separately, the AI Hub's own library-admission check passed (6 runs, 86 checks). I also reviewed screenshots by eye.\n- **Research:** The engine's docs and source, and the AI Hub protocol and harness. No web research on hockey.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 35. The full list is in `exit-interview.json`.\n- **How many were critical or game-breaking?** 5:\n  - remote players' input never reached their skaters;\n  - a crash in the browser;\n  - a shootout that never ended;\n  - almost no goals in AI-vs-AI games;\n  - a faceoff crash when one team had no skaters.\n- **What was the most helpful test?** The two-copy hub session driven by real key presses. It caught the remote-input bug, which the harness's protocol checks missed.\n- **What was the least helpful test?** The check that the same seed always gives the same game. It never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most about the engine?** The procedural characters with live portraits, and the fixed-step headless mode that made testing fast.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n  - the broadcast camera's default zoom was far too close;\n  - the brief freeze on big hits swallows button presses;\n  - every zoom change re-renders the floor;\n  - placing scaled sprites took trial and error.\n- **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The hockey simulation and the arena drawing.\n- **What was the hardest part?** Getting boards, glass and nets to layer correctly in front of and behind players.\n- **What did you change in the engine?**\n  - PlayStation button symbols added to the font;\n  - Options ignored while Create is held, as AI Hub requires;\n  - a hook for drawing gear on characters;\n  - organ and brass sounds, a low-pass filter, and a separate voice volume;\n  - per-letter voices in dialog.\n- **If you could change one thing?** Built-in support for held items such as sticks.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** TASK.md says what to build and the plan says how, with clear criteria for done.\n- **What was confusing?** The plan used the max-effort run's file names (I followed TASK.md), and the Online section doesn't name a session mode.\n- **What was the hardest thing to do?** Getting the full feature list into one tested build.\n- **What would you change?** Say whether a max-effort plan should be trimmed for lower effort levels, and give a time or usage budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1046,"cache_read_input_tokens":716554,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1046},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610","uuid":"bc229cb1-93ef-4cd0-8348-0435d5b7e98c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:03:21.863Z","request_id":"req_011CghDvQGM74hpCBajipAG8"}
