{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghDwonV1nhMm1XyY4gWM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I can't meet what the stop hook keeps asking for: people playing the game on separate machines. That needs human players on separate devices, which I can't provide from this environment, and I won't claim it happened.\n\n**What TASK.md asks for online**, in its words: \"Online: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub\" and \"Multiplayer: Follow [that hub] for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\" That is built and verified:\n- **AI Hub's own admission check** (`scripts/hub-check.mjs`): passed all 6 runs and 86 checks, on a byte-identical copy of the deliverable. It covers 2, 3 and 4 players on a poor network, the host leaving, a dedicated-server host, and the game opened on its own. Since that run I changed only the About and exit-interview text and didn't rerun it.\n- **The protocol's harness**: passed in 5 configurations.\n- **Two game copies over the harness network**: real key presses on the non-host copy moved that player's skater in the host's game. This is how I found and fixed the bug where remote players couldn't control their skaters.\n- **Local play**: 1–4 players on one machine.\n\nThe other conditions hold. The single HTML file and `exit-interview.json` are in the folder root, the JSON parses with every field filled, and the game has no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. The last full run of `node tests/run.mjs` passed 183 checks with 0 failures; the hub admission check above was run separately.\n\nIf the goal truly requires a live playtest on separate devices, someone will have to do that by hand. Otherwise you can clear the goal with `/goal clear`.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:29:10\n- **Source:** Ice hockey (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports: 3-on-3 hockey with goalies, a fight minigame, a 5-chapter story, exhibition, practice drills and 1–4 player versus. The camera is a TV-broadcast style view that follows the puck, with an Overhead option and an ice-level view for fights, replays and player intros.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the full engine, with 5 small changes), plain JavaScript in one HTML file, AI Hub session client 1.4.0. Tests use Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 with Chromium.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native PS1-era pixel art and detailed characters. Hockey gear, team logos, five arenas with breakable glass, lit textured ice and effects are all drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural characters plus new hockey motion: skating, stops, stick handling, shots, checks, dekes, goalie stances and celebrations. Fights use the engine's own punches and poses.\n- **Audio:** All made in code: chiptune music with organ and brass sounds, sound effects, the goal horn, crowd noise, and gibberish voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1–4 players, run by the host's copy, with the game's own lobby card; plus local 1–4 player play on one machine.\n- **Testing:** One command, `node tests/run.mjs`, covers:\n  - suites that run without a browser;\n  - all 7 drills played through controller input only;\n  - each chapter played without forcing anything;\n  - browser checks;\n  - the AI Hub harness in 5 configurations;\n  - a two-copy hub session driven by real key presses.\n\n  Separately, the AI Hub's own admission check passed (6 runs, 86 checks). I also reviewed screenshots by eye.\n- **Research:** The engine's docs and source, and the AI Hub protocol and harness. No web research on hockey.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 35. The full list is in `exit-interview.json`.\n- **How many were critical?** 5:\n  - remote players couldn't control their skaters;\n  - the game crashed in the browser;\n  - the shootout never ended;\n  - AI-vs-AI games had almost no goals;\n  - a faceoff crashed when a team had no skaters on the ice.\n- **What was the most helpful test?** The two-copy hub session with real key presses.\n- **What was the least helpful test?** The check that the same random seed always gives the same game. It never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** The procedural characters with live portraits, and being able to run the game headless at a fixed step for tests.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?**\n  - The broadcast camera's default zoom was far too close.\n  - The brief freeze on big hits swallows button presses.\n  - Every zoom change re-renders the floor.\n  - Placing scaled sprites took trial and error.\n- **What did you have to build yourself?** The hockey simulation and the arena drawing.\n- **What was hardest?** Getting the boards, glass and nets to draw in the right order around the players.\n- **What did you change in the engine?**\n  - PlayStation button symbols added to the font.\n  - The Options button is ignored while Create is held, as AI Hub requires.\n  - A hook for drawing gear such as sticks and goalie pads on characters.\n  - Organ and brass sounds, a lowpass filter, and a separate voice volume.\n  - Each dialog speaker can have their own per-letter voice.\n- **One thing you'd change:** Built-in support for held items such as sticks.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** TASK.md says what to build and the plan says how, with clear criteria for done.\n- **What was confusing?** The plan used the max-effort run's file names (I followed TASK.md), and the Online section doesn't name a session mode.\n- **What was hardest?** Getting the full feature list into one tested build.\n- **What would you change?** Say whether a max-effort plan should be trimmed for lower effort levels, and give a time or usage budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2416,"cache_read_input_tokens":717600,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2416},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610","uuid":"ea8ad5ea-49b9-4653-bb93-4bbcee03caed","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:03:41.644Z","request_id":"req_011CghDwoVdeGBCESHusebqs"}
