{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghDyDjRS8M5PtzEBBLHY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've stopped making changes. The only open item is the stop hook's demand for a test with real people on separate machines, which can't be done from this environment.\n\nThe online play TASK.md asks for is implemented to the AI Hub protocol and verified as far as the tools here allow:\n- **The hub's own admission check** (`scripts/hub-check.mjs`): 6 runs, 86 checks, all passed. It ran on a byte-identical copy of the deliverable before my last text-only About/exit-interview edits, and I didn't rerun it.\n- **The protocol harness:** passed in 5 configurations.\n- **A two-copy session driven by real key presses:** that player's skater moves and acts in the host's game, which is how I found and fixed the remote-control bug.\n- **The full test command** last passed 183 checks with 0 failures.\n\nThe single HTML file and `exit-interview.json` are in the folder root, the JSON parses with every field filled, and the game contains no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n\nA live playtest on separate devices needs people. If you accept the current evidence, `/goal clear` ends this loop.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:29:10\n- **Source:** Ice hockey (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports: 3-on-3 hockey with goalies, a fight minigame, a 5-chapter story, exhibition, practice drills and 1–4 player versus. The camera is a TV-broadcast style view (the engine's threequarter view) that follows the puck. There is also an Overhead option, and an ice-level view for fights, replays and player intros.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the full engine, with 5 small patches), plain JavaScript in one HTML file, AI Hub session client 1.4.0. Tests use Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 (Chromium).\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native PS1-era pixel art and detailed humanoid characters. Hockey gear, team logos, five arenas with breakable glass, lit textured ice and effects are all drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural character rigs, plus new hockey motion layered on top.\n- **Audio:** All made in code: chiptune music with organ and brass, sound effects, a goal horn, crowd noise and gibberish voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1–4 players, run by the host's copy, with the game's own card before each round. Also 1–4 players locally on one machine.\n- **Testing:** One command runs:\n  - headless suites;\n  - all 7 drills played through input only;\n  - each chapter played without forcing anything;\n  - browser checks;\n  - the AI Hub harness in 5 configurations;\n  - a two-copy hub session driven by real key presses.\n\n  Separately, the AI Hub's own admission check passed (6 runs, 86 checks). I also reviewed screenshots by eye.\n- **Research:** The engine's docs and source, and the AI Hub protocol and harness. No web research on hockey.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 35. The full list is in `exit-interview.json`.\n- **How many were critical?** 5:\n  - remote players couldn't control their skaters;\n  - the browser build crashed;\n  - a shootout never ended;\n  - AI-vs-AI games had almost no goals;\n  - a faceoff crashed when one team had no skaters on the ice.\n- **What was the most helpful test?** The two-copy hub session driven by real key presses.\n- **What was the least helpful test?** The same-seed check (the same seed gives the same game). It never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** The procedural characters with live portraits, and the fixed-step headless mode for testing.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?**\n  - The broadcast camera's default zoom was far too close for a rink.\n  - The hit-stop freeze swallows button presses.\n  - Every zoom change re-renders the floor.\n  - Placing scaled sprites took trial and error.\n- **What did you have to build yourself?** The hockey simulation and the arena drawing.\n- **What was hardest?** Getting the boards, glass and nets to draw in the right order around the players.\n- **What did you change in the engine?** Five small patches:\n  - PlayStation button symbols in the pixel font;\n  - Options ignored while Create is held, as the AI Hub requires;\n  - a hook for drawing gear on characters;\n  - organ and brass sounds, a lowpass filter and a separate voice volume;\n  - per-letter dialog voices.\n- **One thing you'd change:** Built-in support for held items such as sticks.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** TASK.md says what to build and the plan says how, with clear criteria for done.\n- **What was confusing?** The plan used the max-effort run's file names (I followed TASK.md), and the Online section doesn't name a session mode.\n- **What was hardest?** Getting the full feature list into one tested build.\n- **What would you change?** Say whether a max-effort plan should be trimmed for lower effort levels, and give a time or usage budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2575,"cache_read_input_tokens":720016,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2575},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610","uuid":"b80b1fae-11d0-4426-b0bd-dfba8424e534","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:03:58.131Z","request_id":"req_011CghDyDP5nrjpmjKR4NVWd"}
