{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghDzU4f7HxmBuzUyA8vA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The stop hook is asking for the same thing again, and I can't provide it: a test where people play online on separate devices. There's no new work I can do toward that from here, so I've made no further changes.\n\nEverything else the goal lists is in place:\n- **Game file:** the single HTML file is in the folder root.\n- **Interview:** `exit-interview.json` parses, with every field filled.\n- **Feature list:** every TASK.md feature is built, with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n- **Online:** built to the AI Hub's own integration rules. It passed the hub's admission check (6 runs, 86 checks, on an identical copy of the game) and its test harness in 5 setups. A two-copy session driven by real key presses also played correctly.\n- **Tests:** the full test command last passed 183 checks with 0 failures.\n\n**Decision for you:** a live playtest with people on separate devices has to be done by hand. If you're satisfied with the evidence above, run `/goal clear` to end this loop.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:29:10\n- **Source:** Ice hockey (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports: 3-on-3 hockey with goalies, a fight minigame, a 5-chapter story, exhibition, practice drills and 1–4 player versus. The camera is a TV-broadcast style view that follows the puck, with an Overhead option and an ice-level view for fights, replays and intros.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2, the full engine with 5 small patches; plain JavaScript in one HTML file; AI Hub session client 1.4.0. Tests use Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 (Chromium).\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's PS1-era pixel art and detailed characters, plus hockey gear, team logos, five arenas, breakable glass and lit ice, all drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural characters, plus hockey motion I added (skating, stick handling, shots, goalie saves, celebrations).\n- **Audio:** All made in code: chiptune music with organ and brass sounds, sound effects, the goal horn, crowd noise and gibberish voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1–4 players, run by the host's copy, with the game's own pre-round card; plus local 1–4 player play.\n- **Testing:** One command runs:\n  - headless suites;\n  - all 7 drills played through input only;\n  - each chapter played without forcing events;\n  - browser checks;\n  - the AI Hub harness in 5 setups;\n  - a two-copy hub session driven by real key presses.\n\n  Separately, the AI Hub's own admission check passed (6 runs, 86 checks), and I reviewed screenshots by eye.\n- **Research:** The engine's docs and source, and the AI Hub protocol and harness. No web research on hockey.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 35; the full list is in `exit-interview.json`.\n- **How many were critical?** 5:\n  - remote players couldn't control their skaters online;\n  - the game crashed in the browser;\n  - the shootout never ended;\n  - AI-vs-AI games had almost no goals;\n  - a faceoff crashed when a team had no skaters on the ice.\n- **What was the most helpful test?** The two-copy hub session driven by real key presses.\n- **What was the least helpful test?** The check that the same random seed always gives the same game. It never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most about the engine?** The procedural characters with live portraits, and the fixed-step headless mode for testing.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?**\n  - The broadcast view's default zoom was far too close.\n  - The hit-stop freeze swallows button presses.\n  - Every zoom change re-renders the floor.\n  - Positioning scaled sprites took trial and error.\n- **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The hockey simulation and the arena drawing.\n- **What was the hardest part?** Getting the boards, glass and nets to draw in the right order around the players.\n- **What did you change in the engine?** Five patches:\n  - PlayStation button symbols in the font;\n  - Options ignored while Create is held, as AI Hub requires;\n  - a hook for drawing gear on characters;\n  - organ and brass sounds, a lowpass filter, and a separate voice volume;\n  - per-letter dialog voices.\n- **If you could change one thing about the engine?** Built-in support for held items such as sticks.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most about this prompt?** TASK.md says what to build, the plan says how, and the criteria for done are clear.\n- **What was confusing?** The plan used the max-effort run's file names (I followed TASK.md), and the Online section doesn't name a session mode.\n- **What was the hardest thing to do?** Getting the full feature list into one tested build.\n- **What would you change?** Say whether a max-effort plan should be trimmed for lower effort levels, and give a time or usage budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2232,"cache_read_input_tokens":722591,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2232},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610","uuid":"0fdd0ec5-fc96-48e9-b0d0-f23ccd1d7744","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:04:14.663Z","request_id":"req_011CghDzTnYrn7ooA5qyDc3Y"}
