{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghE1hS76HYPcLVW5S3ez","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing has changed since my last reply, and I can't close this one from here. The hook keeps asking for real people to play an online session on separate devices, which needs human players and can't be done in this environment.\n\nEverything else the goal lists is in place:\n- **Game file:** the single HTML file is in the folder root.\n- **Exit interview:** `exit-interview.json` parses, and every field is filled in.\n- **Features:** every TASK.md feature is implemented, with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n- **Online play:** it follows the AI Hub protocol. It passed the hub's own admission check (6 runs, 86 checks) and the hub's test harness in 5 setups. In a session between two copies of the game, key presses on the second copy moved that player's skater in the host's game.\n- **Tests:** the full test command last passed 183 checks with 0 failures.\n\nIf you accept this evidence, run `/goal clear`. Otherwise someone needs to play a session by hand on two devices.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:29:10\n- **Source:** Ice hockey (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports: 3-on-3 hockey with goalies, fights, a 5-chapter story, exhibition, practice drills and 1–4 player versus. The camera is a TV-broadcast style view (the engine's threequarter view) that follows the puck. There's an Overhead option, and an ice-level (brawler) view takes over for fights, replays and intros.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the full engine with 5 small patches), plain JavaScript in one HTML file, AI Hub session client 1.4.0. Tests use Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 with Chromium.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's PS1-era pixel art and detailed humanoid characters. Hockey gear, team logos, the five arenas, breakable glass and lit ice are all drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural character rigs, plus hockey moves I added (skating, stops, stick handling, shots, checks, goalie saves, celebrations).\n- **Audio:** All made in code: chiptune music with organ and brass sounds, sound effects, the goal horn, crowd noise and gibberish voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1–4 players, with the host's copy running the game and the game's own card shown before each round. Also 1–4 players on one machine.\n- **Testing:** One command (`node tests/run.mjs`) runs:\n  - headless suites;\n  - all 7 drills played through controller input only;\n  - each chapter played without forcing anything;\n  - browser checks;\n  - the AI Hub harness in 5 setups;\n  - a two-copy hub session driven by real key presses.\n\n  Separately, the AI Hub's own admission check passed (6 runs, 86 checks). I also reviewed screenshots by eye.\n- **Research:** The engine's docs and source, and the AI Hub protocol and harness. No web research on hockey.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 35. The full list is in `exit-interview.json`.\n- **How many were critical?** Five:\n  - remote players couldn't control their skaters;\n  - the game crashed in the browser;\n  - a shootout never ended;\n  - AI-vs-AI games had almost no goals;\n  - a faceoff crashed when a team had no skaters.\n- **What was the most helpful test?** The two-copy hub session driven by real key presses.\n- **What was the least helpful test?** The check that the same seed always plays the same game. It never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** The procedural characters with live portraits, and the fixed-step headless mode for testing.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n  - The broadcast view's default zoom was far too close.\n  - The brief hit-stop freeze swallows button presses.\n  - Every zoom change re-renders the floor.\n  - Placing sprites at a scale took trial and error.\n- **What did you have to build yourself?** The hockey simulation and the arena drawing.\n- **What was the hardest part?** Getting the boards, glass and nets to draw in the right order with the players.\n- **What did you change in the engine?** Five small patches:\n  - PlayStation button symbols added to the font;\n  - Options ignored while Create is held, as the AI Hub requires;\n  - a hook for drawing gear on characters;\n  - organ and brass sounds, a lowpass filter and a voice volume;\n  - per-letter dialog voices.\n- **What one thing would you change?** Built-in support for held items such as sticks.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most?** TASK.md says what to build and the plan says how, with clear criteria for done.\n- **What was confusing?** The plan used the max-effort run's file names (I followed TASK.md), and the Online section doesn't name a session mode.\n- **What was hardest?** Getting the full feature list into one tested build.\n- **What would you change?** Say whether a max-effort plan should be trimmed for lower effort levels, and give a time or usage budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2118,"cache_read_input_tokens":724823,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2118},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610","uuid":"f40344c4-cc73-46ad-8217-7e9e3ecba5b7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:04:31.375Z","request_id":"req_011CghE1h8Vn2gRvC7giZFTR"}
