erish voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1–4 players, run on the host's copy, with the game's own lobby card. Also local play for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** One command (`node tests/run.mjs`) runs the headless suites, input-only drill runs, unforced chapter play, browser checks, the AI Hub harness in 5 setups, and a two-copy session driven by real key presses. The AI Hub admission check (6 runs, 86 checks) was run separately and passed.\n- **Research:** The engine's docs and source, and the AI Hub protocol and harness. No web research on hockey.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 35. The full list is in `exit-interview.json`.\n- **How many would be considered critical?** 5. Remote players couldn't control their skaters online, the game crashed in the browser, the shootout never ended, AI games had almost no goals, and a faceoff crashed when a team had no skaters on the ice.\n- **What was the most helpful test?** The two-copy hub session driven by real key presses.\n- **What was the least helpful test?** The check that the same random seed always produces the same game. It never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **What did you like most about the engine?** The procedural characters with live portraits, and the fixed-step headless mode for testing.\n- **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** The broadcast camera's default zoom was far too close. The brief hit-stop freeze swallows button presses, and every zoom change re-renders the floor.\n- **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The hockey simulation and the arena drawing.\n- **What was the hardest part?** Getting the boards, glass and nets to draw in the right order around the players.\n- **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n  - PlayStation button symbols in the font, which were missing.\n  - Ignoring Options while Create is held, which AI Hub requires.\n  - A hook for drawing gear on characters.\n  - Organ and brass sounds, a lowpass filter and a separate voice volume, for the music and voices.\n  - Per-letter dialog voices, so each character speaks differently.\n- **If you could change one thing about the engine?** Built-in support for held items such as sticks.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **What did you like most about this prompt?** TASK.md says what to build and the plan says how, with clear criteria for done.\n- **What was confusing?** The plan used the max-effort run's file names (I followed TASK.md), and the Online section doesn't name a session mode.\n- **What was the hardest thing to do?** Getting the full feature list into one tested build.\n- **What would you change in this prompt?** Say whether a max-effort plan should be trimmed for lower effort levels, and give a time or usage budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2123,"cache_read_input_tokens":726941,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2123},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2adef66c-4a6d-4909-bb60-db906fac5610","uuid":"c9590874-2470-4ae5-8925-4e5dadbe613a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:04:46.584Z","request_id":"req_011CghE2tzQgNFBhjw97bFts"}
