eb research on hockey.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 35.\n- **How many were critical?** 5:\n  - remote players couldn't control their skaters;\n  - the game crashed in the browser;\n  - the shootout never ended;\n  - AI games had almost no goals;\n  - a faceoff crashed when one team had no skaters.\n- **Most helpful test:** The two-copy hub session driven by real key presses.\n- **Least helpful test:** The same-seed determinism check, which never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The procedural characters and the headless fixed-step mode.\n- **Got stuck or guessed wrong:** The default camera zoom was far too close, the hit-stop freeze swallowed key presses, and every zoom change re-renders the floor.\n- **Built myself:** The hockey simulation and the arena drawing.\n- **Hardest part:** Getting the boards, glass and nets to draw in the right order around the players.\n- **Engine changes:**\n  - PlayStation button symbols added to the font;\n  - Options ignored while Create is held, as AI Hub requires;\n  - a hook for drawing gear on characters;\n  - organ and brass sounds, a low-pass filter and a separate voice bus;\n  - per-letter dialog voices.\n- **One change I'd make:** Built-in support for held items such as sticks.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** A clear split between what to build and how, with clear criteria for done.\n- **Confusing:** The plan's file names didn't match TASK.md's. The Online section doesn't name a session mode.\n- **Hardest:** Fitting the full feature list into one tested build.\n- **Would change:** Say how to scale a max-effort plan for lower effort levels, and give a time or usage budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens