{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghE512c1nUpxWJqKfkY7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've made no changes. The goal is blocked only on a test I can't run here: people playing an online match from separate devices.\n\nEverything else the goal asks for is in place. The single HTML file is in the folder root, `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled, and the game has no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. Online play passes the AI Hub's own admission check (86 checks) and its test harness (5 setups). A session between two copies of the game also works when driven by real key presses.\n\nTo finish, run `/goal clear` if that's enough, or have someone play a session by hand on two devices.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:29:10\n- **Source:** Ice hockey (over-the-top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade 3-on-3 hockey (story, exhibition, drills, versus); a TV-broadcast camera, with an overhead option and an ice-level camera.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (patched), JavaScript in one HTML file, AI Hub session client 1.4.0; tests use Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's PS1-era pixel art, plus hockey art drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural rigs plus custom hockey motion.\n- **Audio:** All made in code: music, sound effects, crowd and gibberish voices.\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions for 1–4 players; local play for 1–4.\n- **Testing:** One command runs headless suites, input-only drills, unforced chapter play, browser checks, the hub harness and a two-copy session. The AI Hub admission check passed separately.\n- **Research:** The engine and AI Hub docs; no web research on hockey.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 35.\n- **How many were critical?** 5:\n  - remote players couldn't control their skaters;\n  - the game crashed in the browser;\n  - a shootout never ended;\n  - there were almost no goals;\n  - a faceoff crashed when a team had no skaters.\n- **Most helpful test:** The two-copy hub session driven by real key presses.\n- **Least helpful test:** The check that the same seed always gives the same game, which never failed.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The procedural characters and the headless fixed-step mode.\n- **Got stuck or guessed wrong:** The camera zoom, input lost during the brief freeze on hits, and floor re-renders on every zoom change.\n- **Built myself:** The hockey simulation and the arena drawing.\n- **Hardest part:** Drawing boards, glass and nets in the right order around players.\n- **What I changed in the engine:**\n  - PlayStation button symbols in the font;\n  - the hub controller rule (Options ignored while Create is held);\n  - a hook for drawing extra gear on characters;\n  - organ and brass sounds, a lowpass filter and a voice volume bus;\n  - per-letter dialog voices.\n- **One thing I'd change:** Built-in support for held items such as sticks.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** It separates what to build from how, with clear criteria for done.\n- **Confusing:** The plan's file names didn't match TASK.md's, and the Online section doesn't name a mode.\n- **Hardest:** Fitting the full feature list into one tested build.\n- **Would change:** Give guidance on scaling a plan to the effort level, and a time or usage budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1683,"cache_read_input_tokens":731057,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1683},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null